<ContentLayout title="Aurora OS — The foundation of the Aurora ecosystem" description="Aurora OS is the main product of the Aurora ecosystem. It is being built from scratch in Rust and is not publicly released." heading="Aurora OS." lead="The foundation of the Aurora ecosystem. An operating system being built from scratch in Rust, with a focus on security, reliability, privacy and user choice.">
  <section class="section shell content-columns">
    <div><h2>In development. Not released.</h2><p class="content-copy">Aurora OS is not available to install yet. There is no public installer, system image or supported-hardware list. Please do not install unofficial files claiming to be Aurora releases.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/en/downloads/">Release availability <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a></div>
    <div><h2>What Aurora is aiming for</h2><ul class="content-list"><li>A secure foundation for personal computing.</li><li>Privacy and reliability built into the system's design.</li><li>Meaningful control over applications and system behavior.</li><li>An adaptable environment for different users and needs.</li></ul></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section shell article-content">
    <h2>Built as part of a wider ecosystem</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">Aurora OS is the central product. Lumen, the Aurora Browser, is being developed as a companion application. The wider goal is for the system and its applications to feel coherent without forcing every component to share the same release schedule.</p>
    <h2>Technical direction</h2>
    <p class="content-copy">Aurora is being developed in Rust, following a capability-based microkernel direction. This describes the project's current architectural direction, not a promise that every planned security or isolation property is already available in a released system.</p>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>